  "敷红、黑、黄三彩上漆；和尚面具宽脸长耳，细眉细目，似笑非笑，额头雕刻有红色福包，为傩戏角色之一，雕刻工艺为浮雕和透雕。面形明显修长，纵向感强，线条层次适中，五官分区明确，左右结构稳定；眉眼和口部处理较柔和，表情倾向含笑、亲近。": "Lacquered in red, black and yellow. This Nuo theatre monk has a broad face, long ears, fine brows and eyes, a faint smile and a red blessing bump on his forehead, carved using relief and openwork techniques. The face is distinctly elongated, with a strong vertical emphasis, the lines have moderate detail and the facial features are clearly separated, the left and right sides are structurally balanced. Softly treated brows, eyes and mouth create a smiling, approachable expression.",
